# In how many countries do women live longer than men?
subtitle: "Sort countries by who lives longer there, then see how big the gap is, where it comes from, and the countries where it once ran the other way."
tags: ["health","data","geography"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Who lives longer, where?\" note \"Women vs men\""

## In how many countries do women live longer than men?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Nigeria
      - India
      - Norway
      - USA
      - Japan
      - Russia
    values:
      - [0.6, 3.1, 3.1, 5, 6.1, 11.8]
      - [4, -1.5, 3.3, 5.6, 3.3, 7.9]
    stage: 0
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - -3
      - 13
    y_label: Women's extra years
    icons:
      - {of: flag nigeria, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag india, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag norway, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag united states, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag japan, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag russia, set: twemoji}
    label_size: 30
    bar_colors: same
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Life expectancy of women vs. life expectancy of men
      authors: Our World in Data, from UN World Population Prospects (2024)
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/life-expectancy-of-women-vs-life-expectancy-of-men
      finding: in 2023 women outlive men in every country; world 75.9 vs 70.5 years; gap 0.6 years in Nigeria, 3.1 in India and Norway, 5.0 in the US, 6.1 in Japan, 11.8 in Russia; in 1950 men lived longer in India (by 1.5 years), Pakistan, Iran and Bangladesh
    - id: owid_why
      title: Why do women live longer than men?
      authors: Saloni Dattani and Lucas Rodés-Guirao (Our World in Data)
      year: 2023
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/why-do-women-live-longer-than-men
      finding: women live longer in all countries; newborn boys die more often than girls; smoking, alcohol, accidents and violence add to men's deaths; until recently men lived longer in India, Bangladesh, Pakistan and Iran
    - id: wpp
      title: World Population Prospects 2024
      authors: United Nations
      year: 2024
      finding: life expectancy at birth by sex, 1950–2023

    cards who cites ["owid"] size 2 x 40 width 920 bins ["Women longer","Men longer"] arrange side hidden true
        * "Russia" icon.of "flag russia" icon.set twemoji bin "Women longer"
        * "Nigeria" icon.of "flag nigeria" icon.set twemoji bin "Women longer"
        * "India" icon.of "flag india" icon.set twemoji bin "Women longer"
        * "Japan" icon.of "flag japan" icon.set twemoji bin "Women longer"
        * "USA" icon.of "flag united states" icon.set twemoji bin "Women longer"
        * "Norway" icon.of "flag norway" icon.set twemoji bin "Women longer"
    path avg dashed thick #8f887c cites ["owid"] points [[-0.45,5.3],[5.45,5.3]] data true hidden true
    text avg_l "world: 5" #8f887c at.data [0.1,6.3] cites ["owid"] font_size 36 hidden true
    text baby "baby boys: more fragile" #2f2b26 cites ["owid_why"] x 500 y 610 font_size 46 hidden true
    text smoke "men: smoking, drink, risk" #2f2b26 cites ["owid_why"] x 500 y 610 font_size 46 hidden true
    text y1950 "1950" #2f2b26 at.data [3.3,10.5] cites ["owid"] font_size 72 hidden true
    text y2023 "2023" #2f2b26 at.data [3.3,10.5] cites ["owid"] font_size 72 hidden true

    card title "Where do women live longer?"

A: In which countries do women live longer than men? Here are six: rich and poor, hot and cold.
    draw who

B: Russia, women for sure. But Nigeria? India? I'd bet men win somewhere in there.
    highlight who_2 who_3

    ask "Sort each country: who lives longer there?" on who store f default "4"
        right: {f} of {f.total}. Women live longer in all six.
        wrong: {f} of {f.total} on the first try. Women win in every one of them.

    erase who

A: In fact, today women outlive men in every country in the world.
    draw axes bar_1 bar_2 bar_3 bar_4 bar_5 bar_6 y2023

A: By about five years on average.
    draw avg avg_l

A: But the gap varies a lot: under a year in Nigeria, almost twelve years in Russia.
    highlight bar_1 bar_6

B: Twelve years? That can't just be biology.
    highlight bar_6

    erase y2023

A: Some of it is. From their first week, baby boys are more fragile than girls.
    draw baby

    erase baby

A: Much of the rest is how men live: more smoking, more drinking, more accidents and violence.
    draw smoke

    erase smoke avg avg_l

    draw y1950

A: And it wasn't always this way. Here are the same six countries in 1950.
    animate stage 1 duration 2.5

B: Hold on. India's bar is below zero. Men lived longer there?
    highlight bar_2

A: By a year and a half. And so did men in Pakistan, Iran and Bangladesh.
    highlight bar_2

    erase y1950

    draw y2023

    animate stage 0 duration 2.5

A: Today Indian women are three years ahead. So the gap is partly biology, and partly something societies can change.
    text shift "India: −1.5 → +3.1" #b5482e at.data [1.4,8.6] cites ["owid"] font_size 52

    highlight shift bar_2

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon w size 280 set twemoji x 250 y 450 icon_look picture of woman hidden true
    icon m size 280 set twemoji x 750 y 450 icon_look picture of man hidden true
    text vs "vs" #8f887c x 500 y 460 font_size 110 hidden true
    thumb band "Who lives longer? Where?" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon globe size 300 set twemoji x 260 y 440 icon_look picture of "globe showing europe-africa" hidden true
    text t1 "? of 200" #b5482e x 690 y 480 font_size 130 hidden true
    text t2 "countries" #2f2b26 x 690 y 350 font_size 70 hidden true
    thumb band "Women live longer in…" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon f1 size 230 set twemoji x 260 y 450 icon_look picture of "flag india" hidden true
    text y "1950" #2f6b8f x 680 y 500 font_size 150 hidden true
    text q "Who lived longer?" #2f2b26 x 640 y 340 font_size 64 hidden true
    thumb band "India, 1950" kind band hidden true
